---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { formulas } from '../../lib/formulas';
const tasks = [...new Set(formulas.map(item => item.task))];
---
<Base title="Excel & Google Sheets Formula Finder" description="Find curated Excel and Google Sheets formulas by task, with sample inputs, expected results, product differences and official documentation." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Tools',url:'/tools/'},{name:'Formula Finder',url:'/tools/formula-finder/'}]}>
  <div>
    <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Find a starting point</p><h1>Formula Finder</h1><p>Eight everyday functions. Choose your spreadsheet app, find your task, and adapt a clear example.</p></header>
    <p class="notice">This is a curated reference, not a calculator. Examples and expected results are static. No formulas run in Excel or Google Sheets here. English function names and comma separators are shown; your locale may require different names or semicolons.</p>
    <form id="formula-filters" class="panel" role="search">
      <div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="field"><label for="formula-query">Function name or task keyword</label><input id="formula-query" type="search" placeholder="Try XLOOKUP, spaces, or rows" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="formula-product">Spreadsheet app</label><select id="formula-product"><option value="Excel">Excel</option><option value="Google Sheets">Google Sheets</option></select></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="formula-task">Task</label><select id="formula-task"><option value="all">All tasks</option>{tasks.map(task => <option value={task}>{task}</option>)}</select></div>
      </div>
      <button type="reset" class="button secondary">Reset filters</button>
    </form>
    <p id="formula-status" class="status" aria-live="polite">8 formulas. Showing Excel examples.</p>
    <p id="formula-empty" class="notice" hidden>No formulas match. Try a function name or reset the filters.</p>
    <div id="formula-cards" class="tool-grid">
      {formulas.map(item => <article class="panel formula-card" data-name={item.name} data-task={item.task}>
        <span class="chip">{item.task}</span><h2>{item.name}</h2><p>{item.purpose}</p>
        <div data-product="Excel"><h3>Excel syntax</h3><pre><code>{item.excelSyntax}</code></pre><h3>Example to copy</h3><pre><code>{item.excelExample}</code></pre></div>
        <div data-product="Google Sheets" hidden><h3>Google Sheets syntax</h3><pre><code>{item.sheetsSyntax}</code></pre><h3>Example to copy</h3><pre><code>{item.sheetsExample}</code></pre></div>
        <button class="button secondary formula-copy" type="button" data-excel={item.excelExample} data-sheets={item.sheetsExample} aria-label={`Copy ${item.name} example`}>Copy example</button>
        <h3>Sample inputs</h3><p>{item.inputs}</p><h3>Expected output</h3><p>{item.output}</p>
        <h3>Limits and compatibility</h3><p>{item.limits}</p>
        <p>Official documentation: <a href={item.excelSource}>Microsoft {item.name}</a> · <a href={item.sheetsSource}>Google Sheets {item.name}</a></p>
      </article>)}
    </div>
    <section class="prose"><h2>Before you use an example</h2><p>Replace sample ranges with your own cells, keep matching ranges aligned, and test on a small copy of your data. Text such as P02 is an identifier, while the amount examples use actual numeric cells. A correct formula can still produce the wrong answer if your source data has hidden spaces, text-formatted numbers or unexpected blanks.</p><h2>How these examples are checked</h2><p>Syntax and compatibility notes were reviewed against the linked official documentation on October 24, 2026. Automated JavaScript checks cover the simple arithmetic, filtering and text results in these sample fixtures; they do not emulate a spreadsheet engine or verify behavior in a live workbook. Verify results in your target app and version.</p></section>
    <aside class="panel"><h2>Keep learning</h2><p><a class="button secondary" href="/formulas/google-sheets-filter-examples/">Explore Google Sheets FILTER examples</a></p></aside>
    <noscript><p class="notice">All Excel examples are readable without JavaScript. Enable JavaScript to filter, switch app or copy examples.</p></noscript>
  </div>
</Base>
<script>import '../../scripts/formula-finder';</script>
